could anybody tell me how to modify it to work for equivalent goal? THANKS!I see two problems.  First, the quadratic form x^TAxx^TAx is convex only for AA positive semidefinite.  But suppose AA were positive semidefinite (and for simplicity LM\in R^5LM\in R^5).  The second problem is that you would need to use quad_form(LM,A) rather than LM'*A*LM for cvx to recognize it.  See page 60 of the (http://cvxr.com/cvx/cvx_usrguide.pdf).

I’m afraid Bien’s proposal to use quad_form will not work here, at least not immediately, because the quadratic form is not a scalar. The quadratic form CVX is complaining about is LM'*A*LM. This is a 4x4 matrix whose off-diagonal terms violate the DCP ruleset (and besides, they are non-convex). Even though those non-convex terms are eventually discarded by trace(), CVX has no way of knowing that.
However, if AA is positive definite, you can try this: let R = chol(A) be the Cholesky factor of A, so the objective can be rewritten trace(LM'*R'*R*LM). Then this is equivalent to sum_square(R*LM).
Another simple way to handle it is
tmp = 0;
for k = 1 : 4,
    tmp = tmp + LM(:,k)'*A*LM(:,k);
end

In this case, you can use quad_form instead per Bien’s suggestion.

