Thanks for your reply. There are two versions of rel-entr in cvx package, one in cvx\functions and the other in cvx\functions\@cvx. I’ll check on the version in cvx\functions\@cvx.Thanks again for Mark’s suggestion. I reread the user’s guide and found a concept of perspective of a function from (https://web.stanford.edu/~boyd/cvxbook/bv_cvxbook.pdf) (Page 103, 3.2.6). Actually, my function is a perspective of 2^x2^x, thus it’s convex. On the other hand, thanks to the guidance from Michael C. Grant in (//ask.cvxr.com/t/exponential-perspective-function-on-cvx/387), I found a way to develop my own function follows DCP ruleset as follows:
function cvx_optval = myFoo( x, y )
cvx_begin
    variables z;
    minimize( z );
    subject to
        {x * log(2), y, z} == exponential;
cvx_end

